Recovered statistical-analysis script | reproducibility package | Fig. 3 track.

WHAT THIS SCRIPT COMPUTES
    This code takes an already-assembled DataFrame CH, holding a chain of
    pairwise design contrasts, and writes it out unchanged to a CSV file
    in the figure 3 data directory. No computation of means, differences,
    confidence intervals, or p values happens in this snippet itself;
    those values must have been produced earlier in the analysis and are
    simply being saved here. One row of the output table represents a
    single step in a build-up design chain, comparing one model or
    condition configuration to the next, isolating a specific factor that
    changed between them, and reporting the associated summary statistics
    and test results for one metric. With nine rows, the table captures
    nine such successive one-factor comparisons along the chain.

